exp_07 round 2 cycle 1b: per-arm seen controls and protocol-aware build_fields

compare_control now normalises both sides to a protocol (historical args predate
exp_07), derives the expected micro-batch count from that protocol's training-file
count (296 454 for seen), and for a seen arm keeps only the operational exclusions
of plan §2 plus 'protocol' - yaw_aug/yaw_aug_seed/yaw_aug_width/no_save must match
its unseen twin, and a comparator that is not an unseen twin is refused.

build_fields derives the protocol from the argv: it requires the seen dataset
module in the training closure, hashes the seen inventory into its own cache
(ckpt/exp07/train_inventory_seen.json), records 'protocol', binds
mutable_inputs.seen_split (path + sha256 of the authors' pickle) and selects the
per-arm comparator (seen_aug -> exp_04's attempt args, with its recorded env).

